    "created_at": "2022-05-18T17:38:24Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-05-18T17:38:24Z",
    "body": "Note that some RFCs have much nicer versions, e.g.:\r\n\r\n- https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9239.html\r\n- https://httpwg.org/specs/rfc8941.html (although https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8941.html also exists)\r\n\r\nIMO it's pretty important to give our readers links to these nicer versions when possible. So I'd suggest:\r\n\r\n- If an rfc-editor version exists, use that\r\n- Otherwise, if a httpwg version exists, use that\r\n- Otherwise, use the datatracker version\r\n\r\nWe might want to try to get Bikeshed/Specref to take on a similar policy...",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
